le description:  persons.<br>"Delhi in the thirteenth century had grown to be one of the largest cities of the Muslim world. A number of other cities had emerged as major urban centres during this period - Multan, Lahore, Anhilwara, Kara, Kambath, Sonargaon and Lakhnauti, to name a few".<br>Delhi became probably the largest city in South Asia.<br>The population of Gaur, the principal city of Bengal, was estimated at 200,000 persons. Delhi would have a much bigger population than Gaur. . It received large numbers of immigrants from Central Asia and Persia, who were driven there by the Mongol invasions. <br>\n                    '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2187, 'temperature': 0.2})
