ulation estimated at 100,000. This state eroded the highly tribalised nature of Berber society and attained a high degree of civilisation." <br>"Masinissa\'s capital would appear to have grown into a real city (though the population of 200,000 attributed to it under Masinissa\'s son must be a gross exaggeration). The archaeology is not well known but its urban aspect will have been almost entirely Carthaginian".\n                    '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2037, 'temperature': 0.2})
